From b02faea0a9f75e7326ecf3b2305203331a44bd0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:08:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: release a PR owner whose same-second park or
 awaited exact-head review handed it off

Three PR owners sat READY with no worker for 30 min to 2 h until an operator released
them (2026-11-12/13). The active_pr guard missed three handoff shapes:

1. Same second. The owner posts its checkpoint naming the PR and parks with
   kanban_schedule / kanban_continue in one turn. Both rows share a whole-second
   timestamp, and the guard's "handoff strictly after the newest PR comment" refused
   the tie (t_01a1d30035fa4777, PR #1862: comment 15615 and its `scheduled` event
   both at 1794542252). New kanban_pr_same_run_park: the tie counts only when every
   PR comment at that second has exactly one commented event, written by the run
   that parked (portable writer_run_uid on synced schemas), ordered before the park
   event, and that run is the assignee's latest executed run. Dependency parks
   keep their existing server-stamped watermark rule.
2. Awaited, unlinked review. A timed park waiting on a review card (wake_check
   `hermes kanban wait-check task <id>`, or awaiting kind card) is not a parent, so
   resumes_review never saw its approval. New kanban_awaited_review: one
   continuation when the latest executed run is the assignee's orderly
   scheduled/continued park, every awaited card is done with a claimed completion
   after the park, none requested changes, and together they approve every holding
   PR by name at a reviewed_sha equal to the PR's current GitHub head (gh pr view
   headRefOid, OPEN only, cached like pr_state). A change request, other head, other
   or unnamed PR, unknown head, or a crash/reclaim after the park keeps the hold.
3. Historical review parent. A dependency park whose exact-head approval parent
   finished before the park still refused the ordering handoff once the awaited
   rollout parent finished (t_01a1d09d3547337b, state PR #1760: held from
   02:19Z until operator schedule+unblock). Only parents awaited at the park now
   decide that handoff; finished, unchanged ones were already in the owner's
   context (the same rule the code already applied to remote parents).

The fourth shape on the card, a home `kanban resume` that runners ignored
(t_01a1d120e7d7c686, PR #1708), was fixed by 3111eba0fd/7cc74b2d05 (worker-copy
receipt carry), which landed after the card was written; their tests
(test_kanban_operator_resume_worker_copy.py) are the acceptance for it, and a
replay of that card at 3 hold cutoffs on this base returns None.

The decided same-second rule changes 6 expectations in test_kanban_pr_continuation.py:
an invalid watermark or missing checkpoint on a same-run report+continue tie now
resumes once (event order proves it), and each case still asserts the hold once the
comment's provenance is unreadable.

Five whys
Problem: owners READY with no worker 30 min-2 h after their awaited review approved
  (respawn_guarded active_pr on the workers; events on t_01a1d04fee42c1c7 196441).
Why 1: active_pr_reason found no handoff after the newest PR comment.
Why 2: the only handoff was a park in the same second as that comment (case 1), a
  review card that was not a parent (case 2), or a dependency handoff vetoed by a
  pre-park review parent (case 3).
Why 3: the guard compares whole-second timestamps and fails closed on ties; review
  release is defined only over task_links parents; the dependency handoff looped
  over all parents rather than those awaited at the park.
Root (happened): handoff evidence was keyed on clock order and link topology, not
  on the facts that prove intent (same run + event order; the card the park names).
Root (not caught): #1595's tests (test_kanban_pr_comment_provenance) always advanced
  the fake clock between comment and park, and no test parked on an unlinked review
  or combined a pre-park review parent with a later ordering parent; the live shapes
  were never fixtures.
Recurrence: 3rd active_pr follow-up on t_01a1d04fee42c1c7 (#1595 covered only a
  same-run note strictly after the park).

Proof
- RED on the base (pr_state.py at fc4e67e6ec, new modules present): 7 failed, exactly
  the positive cases (same-second x scheduled/continued x local/synced, awaited review
  x wake_check/awaiting, approved-before-park parent). GREEN: all pass (82 in the two
  files).
- Live replays from sync-shadow rows at the hold time: t_01a1d30035fa4777 @1794543185
  active_pr -> None (head stub = reviewed head; other head stays active_pr);
  t_01a1d09d3547337b @1794536343 active_pr -> None; t_01a1d120e7d7c686 None both.
- Replay over read-only copies of every local board and sync-shadow (default, hermes,
  bb, askeve, runners, worker-load) on hermes-worker-1: every orderly park
  (scheduled/continued/dependency_wait) of a card naming a PR in the last 7 days,
  evaluated READY at park+600 s (capped before the next claim), GitHub stubbed OPEN
  and head = the awaited/parent review's reviewed_sha (upper bound on releases).
  3,763 evaluations, 3 changed active_pr -> None, all this class:
  t_01a1d30035fa4777 (case 1/2 above); t_01a1ccbbc5a2ee34 (bb-tuner progress note
  naming me/myapp#3553 and kanban_continue at 1794440517, same run 29818);
  t_01a1cf0f09c93f1e (dependency park on t_01a1cf4be21749c9 after its two
  exact-head approval parents finished at 1794475240/1794476783). Nothing changed
  None -> active_pr; 0 errors.
- Mutants: 33 run over the 3 touched modules (tie id/second/order/writer/assignee,
  unreadable events, awaited/parents loop, hook removal, change-request veto, open
  awaited card, subset cover, head equality, named PR, verdict, outcome, awaiting
  kind/ref, wait-check anchor, gh state/rc/json/cache): 32 killed. 1 equivalent:
  dropping `if not ids` - ids is empty only when every PR comment was restated after
  the latest park, and then no park of that run sits at since (= park - 1).

Card: t_01a1d39b9c475c7b
